meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: Marking progress against child labour - Global estimates and trends 2000-2012
    description: |-
      This report from the International Labour Organization (ILO) presents global and regional estimates of child labor for 2012 and compares them with the earlier estimates for 2000, 2004 and 2008. It covers children aged 5 to 17 in employment, in child labor and in hazardous work, broken down by region, sex, age group, national income and sector of economic activity.

      Table 5 of the report gives the number (in thousands) and share of children in employment, in child labor and in hazardous work by age group: ages 5 to 14 and 15 to 17 for 2000, 2004, 2008 and 2012, and ages 5 to 11 and 12 to 14 for 2012 only.
    date_published: "2013-09-23"
    version_producer: "2012"

    # Citation
    producer: International Labour Organization
    citation_full: |-
      ILO-IPEC. Marking progress against child labour - Global estimates and trends 2000-2012. International Labour Office, International Programme on the Elimination of Child Labour (IPEC). Geneva: ILO, 2013.

